592186045417] [17592186171073 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171073 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "35e0af4c-b666-548c-8eb5-d57899c8f79a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171074 #edb/ref 1080 "-9 \\mid x \\mid" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171074 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171074 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5c02d3c1-17b7-5899-a2f6-bc699f523f27" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171714 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1238" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171714 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify the expression $\\left| - \\dfrac{x^2}{10} \\right|$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171714 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8b27c37f-10a7-5e55-8230-916bb246142b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171714 #edb/ref 1074 "Firstly, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}{-a} & = & a\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nwe can write our expression as\n\n$$\n\\left| \\dfrac{x^2}{10} \\right|\n$$\n\nThen, we distribute the absolute value over the multiplication and division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid \\frac{x^{2}}{10} \\mid &=  \\\\\n\\frac{\\begin{vmatrix}x^{2} &}{\\mid 10\\end{vmatrix}} &=  \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\mid x^{2} \\mid}{10}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince\n\n$$\nx^2 \\geq 0\n$$\n\nfor any real $x$, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left|x^2\\right &= x^2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{\\mid x^{2} \\mid}{10} &= \\frac{x^{2}}{10}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171715 #edb/ref 1069 "e-1239" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171715 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $x\\lt 0$, simplify $\\mid {-6x} \\mid +2x$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171715 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e0d4030c-4490-5e36-af26-7ded6003e841" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171715 #edb/ref 1074 "Firstly, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}{-a} & = & a\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nwe can write our expression as\n\n$$\n\\mid 6x \\mid +2x\n$$\n\nThen, we distribute the absolute value over the multiplication. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid 6x \\mid + 2x &=  \\\\\n\\begin{vmatrix}6 & \\cdot & x\\end{vmatrix}+ 2x &=  \\\\\n6 \\cdot\\begin{vmatrix}x & + 2x &= \\\\ 6 & x\\end{vmatrix}+ 2x \\mid\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $x \\lt 0$, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid x &= -x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6 \\mid x\\begin{vmatrix}+ 2x &= \\\\ 6(-x) + 2x|= \\\\ -6x + 2x|= \\\\ -4x\\end{vmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171819 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6800" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171819 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify the expression $\\begin{vmatrix}{-3z} & -5\\cdot & 4z\\end{vmatrix}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171819 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9c4b5b23-3d35-593a-ae69-4766e5b1d996" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186171819 #edb/ref 1074 "Firstly, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}{-a} & = & a\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nwe can write our expression as\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}3z & -5\\cdot & 4z\\end{vmatrix}\n$$\n\nThen, we distribute the absolute value over the multiplication, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}3z & -5 \\cdot & 4z\\end{vmatrix} &=  \\\\\n\\begin{vmatrix}3 & \\cdot & z & -5 \\cdot & 4 & \\cdot & z\\end{vmatrix} &=  \\\\\n3 \\cdot\\begin{vmatrix}z & -5 \\cdot 4 \\cdot & z & &= \\\\ 3 \\cdot & z & -20 \\cdot & z\\end{vmatrix}|= \\\\\n3\\begin{vmatrix}z & -20 & z\\end{vmatrix} &=  \\\\\n&= - 17 \\mid z \\mid\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172015 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048159 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172015 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050452 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172015 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186172573 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172015 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186172574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172015 #edb/ref 1039 "Simplifying Absolute Value Expressions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172015 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186171819 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172015 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "72810e1e-8a12-5488-8aac-3a94cc027e68" #edb/ref 17592