/ref 17592186171069 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172574 #edb/ref 1069 "q-52129" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172574 #edb/ref 1071 "Simplify the expression $\\begin{vmatrix}-5x & -2 \\cdot & -2x\\end{vmatrix}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172574 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7a58b47f-7007-5bd7-bf0e-68281bd0b768" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172867 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186173102 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172867 #edb/ref 1061 25123 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172867 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4c2ee3dc-ab94-51f0-bcdc-ab20413c5355" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186172867 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186172015 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173015 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186172867 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173015 #edb/ref 1061 36685 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173015 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "de7a2169-7d86-5d52-813f-d1d199541882" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173015 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186173210 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173035 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186173103 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173035 #edb/ref 1061 3977 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173035 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a35c659d-3a92-5292-a856-8e051b0df01d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173035 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186172111 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173036 #edb/ref 1061 3978 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173036 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6c3441ba-31e5-52c4-9a8b-3e8a4cd3a43d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173036 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186172112 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173102 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186173035 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173102 #edb/ref 1061 5019 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173102 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f329f688-b5f5-5222-a1c0-599debe7606f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173102 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186173140 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173103 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186173036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173103 #edb/ref 1061 5922 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173103 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3819c50d-8c6b-5e33-b8c9-e35bd4855c00" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173103 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186173141 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173140 #edb/ref 1064 "We know that the absolute value operation does nothing to a number if it is non-negative. For example:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid 0 \\mid &= 0 \\\\\n\\mid 1 \\mid &= 1 \\\\\n\\mid 2 \\mid &= 2 \\\\\n\\mid 3 \\mid &= 3 \\\\\n&= ⋮\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can summarize this fact as follows:\n\n$$\n\\mid x \\mid = x \\quad \\text{if} \\quad x \\geq 0\n$$\n\nWe also know that $x^2$ is non-negative for any value of $x$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\left|x^2\\right| = x^2\n$$\n\nwhere $x$ is *any* real number." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173140 #edb/ref 1065 1716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173140 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "b20a7fe3-4627-5ed7-a7dd-afd383fa3c59" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173140 #edb/ref 1067 "The Absolute Value of a Square" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173141 #edb/ref 1064 "We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid x &= x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nif\n\n$$\nx \\geq 0\n$$\n\nBut what if $x < 0$?\n\nIf a variable is known to be negative, then the absolute value changes it to positive. To turn a negative number into a positive number, we multiply by $-1$. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\mid x \\mid = -x \\quad\\textrm{for}\\quad x < 0\n$$\n\nTo convince ourselves that this is indeed true, let's verify it in the case when $x=-2$. Substituting this value into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid - 2 \\mid &= - (-2) = 2.✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173141 #edb/ref 1065 1831 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173141 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "93c4f77c-611c-5870-88b3-e76b8bbc7275" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173141 #edb/ref 1067 "The Absolute Value of a Negative Variable" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173210 #edb/ref 1064 "In this lesson, we'll extend our knowledge of absolute value.\n\nLet's first remind ourselves of the rules of absolute value:\n\n- $\\begin{vmatrix}{-a} & = & a\\end{vmatrix}$\n- $\\begin{vmatrix}a \\cdot b & = & a & \\cdot & b\\end{vmatrix}$\n- $\\left| \\dfrac{a}{b} \\right| = \\dfrac{\\begin{vmatrix}a &}{\\mid b\\end{vmatrix}}$\n\nRecall that the last two rules are known as the **distributive properties.**" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173210 #edb/ref 1065 6010 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173210 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "3d23d2e9-6bc0-5a8b-bdb3-84a2f0e9d4d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186173210 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
